---
interface Props {
  role: string;
  company: string;
}
const { role, company } = Astro.props;
---

<section id="about" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
  <div style="max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 96px 48px;">
    <div
      data-reveal
      class="overline"
      style="margin-bottom: 24px; padding-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);"
    >
      <span data-i18n>About</span>
    </div>
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: flex-start;">
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2
          style="font: 500 clamp(30px, 3.4vw, 44px)/1.1 'Poppins', sans-serif; letter-spacing: -0.03em; color: var(--text-bright); margin: 0; text-wrap: balance;"
        >
          <span data-i18n>I design so users struggle less and teams guess less.</span>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 120ms; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;">
        <p data-i18n style="font: 400 16px/26px 'Poppins', sans-serif; color: var(--text-primary); margin: 0;">
          I see design as a way to help people. Good software makes their work and life lighter, so my job is to understand what they need before I draw anything. That's why I say no more often than yes. In data-heavy products with complex flows, every feature has a cost: users learn more, teams maintain more. I decide what to keep, what to cut, and I can explain why to both PMs and engineers.
        </p>
        <p data-i18n style="font: 400 16px/26px 'Poppins', sans-serif; color: var(--text-primary); margin: 0;">
          With AI, I work on both sides. In my own process, I automate repetitive work to leave time for the hard decisions. In products, I design so AI takes over the manual steps while users keep the final say and a way back when AI gets it wrong.
        </p>
        <p data-i18n style="font: 400 16px/26px 'Poppins', sans-serif; color: var(--text-primary); margin: 0;">
          I don't just deliver screens. On the centralized document management system I helped design, users retrieve documents 30% faster, access rights are clearer, and the whole system was handed over in one month with user training so the team could run it on their own.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/about"
          data-cursor="hover"
          class="btn btn--primary" style="margin-top: 24px; align-self: flex-start;"
        >
          <span data-i18n>View profile</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
